==Battleground==
*3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 6 seconds<sup>180f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 16 seconds<sup>480f</sup>, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*6 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Easter Egg Cat (Enemy)|Easter Egg Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**2 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] will be your main meatshield here due to the Angels, along with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|any]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Eraser]] for Easter Egg Cat. Angelic Slepnir will keep pressure on your units, but due to the Egg's relatively low Omni Strike and high health, you can stack [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] to hit him behind the frontlines. Any Uber that has an ability against [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|Angels]] and/or [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Traitless]], while also outranging Easter Egg Cat will do well here. You can fill the rest of your slots with attackers with above 300+ range such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] or [[Cat Combo]]s.

